    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1163">

                <pb facs="0956" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/964a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Consul and Vice Consul at Nogales, the
                            Consular Agent at Cananea, and the Consul at
                    Hermosillo</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Say to the Americans who have been supplied with arms for their self-defense that
                    the arms are furnished them solely for the protection <pb facs="0957" n="841"
                        xml:id="pg841"/> of their lives and that they should most carefully guard
                    against any indiscreet acts; point out the disastrous effects such acts would
                    undoubtedly have upon their own interests and upon the lives and property of
                    Americans elsewhere in Mexico; remind them finally of the responsibility resting
                    upon them in this respect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
